{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "bc038b20-1f7f-4f4b-8350-a0caef008703",
    "name": "e-MART API (Modules 1-9)",
    "description": "e-MART backend - all 9 modules.\n\n## Quick start\n1. Run `emart_schema.sql` then `emart_seed_data.sql`.\n2. Start the app: `mvnw.cmd clean spring-boot:run`\n3. Run **02 Auth > Login (cardholder)** first - it saves the JWT into the\n   `accessToken` collection variable automatically. Every other request\n   inherits it via Bearer auth.\n\n## Seed logins (password is `Password@123` for all)\n| Email | Notes |\n|---|---|\n| rishi.chhalotre@example.com | approved cardholder, 350 pts -> cardholder pricing |\n| ananya.sharma@example.com | normal member -> MRP pricing |\n| priya.nair@example.com | inactive -> login refused |\n\n## Mock payment gateway\nA card number ending in **0** is DECLINED. Anything else is approved.\nUse `4242424242424242` to succeed, `4242424242424240` to test failure.\n\n## Suggested end-to-end run\nLogin -> Add to cart -> Checkout preview -> Place order -> Verify payment\n-> Download invoice PDF.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{accessToken}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
